Subject: [PATCH 27/30] ChunkBlockHashMap: H01 parts 2 and 3 behind
 chunkmap.cache4Seguro

With the key on (default off = original code at these three points):
- get: on a miss, only the server thread writes last1..last4; any other
  thread returns what it found in the map without writing.
- remove: clears every slot whose coordinates match the chunk and packs the
  rest in order. The original assumes at most one match: with [F, A, A, C]
  it leaves A in the second slot and get() keeps returning the unloaded chunk.
- put: drops any slot with the same coordinates before pushing the new chunk,
  so the cache never holds two slots for one coordinate.
No method calls inside the slot updates. Independent of chunkmap.ligado.

